1.Subdomain Enumeration:Amass (Ya Subfinder).Sabse pehle target ke saare subdomains dhoondhein aur unhe bina kisi kachre ke ek file mein save karein.Bashamass enum -d target.com
amass subs -d target.com -names -silent | sort -u > all_subdomains.txt
(Pro-tip: Amass slow lage toh aap subfinder -d target.com -silent | sort -u > all_subdomains.txt bhi use kar sakte hain).
2.DNS Resolution (Zinda IPs filter karein):dnsx.In subdomains mein se pata lagayein ki kiske paas asli IP address hai aur kaun dead hai. Slow speed aur multiple resolvers ka use karein taaki drop na ho.Bashcat all_subdomains.txt | dnsx -silent -t 20 -retry 3 -r 8.8.8.8,1.1.1.1,9.9.9.9 | sort -u > resolving_subdomains.txt
3.Find Dead Domains & Test Takeovers:grep + nuclei.Total list mein se resolving wale hata kar Dead Subdomains nikalein, aur unpar Subdomain Takeover check karein.Bashgrep -v -x -f resolving_subdomains.txt all_subdomains.txt > dead_subdomains.txt
nuclei -l dead_subdomains.txt -t takeovers/ -o takeover_bugs.txt
4.Filter Live Web Targets:httpx.Resolving IPs mein se wo targets nikalein jinpar Website (Port 80/443) chal rahi hai. Isey aap baad mein XSS, SQLi aadi ke liye use karenge.Bashcat resolving_subdomains.txt | httpx -silent -status-code -title -tech-detect > live_websites.txt
(Next step ke liye ek clean list bhi bana lein jisme se https:// hata ho):Bash cat resolving_subdomains.txt | httpx -silent | sed 's/https\?:\/\///' | sort -u > web_only.txt
5.Extract Non-Web Targets:grep.Resolving subdomains mein se Web wale hata dein, taaki sirf hidden infrastructure (Databases, FTP, SSH) wale targets bachein.Bashgrep -v -x -f web_only.txt resolving_subdomains.txt > non_web_targets.txt
6.Scan for Hidden Open Ports:naabu.Non-web targets par top 1000 ports scan karein taaki open databases aur services ka pata chal sake.Bashnaabu -l non_web_targets.txt -top-ports 1000 -c 50 -silent -o open_ports.txt
7.Hunt for Network Bugs & Default Logins:nuclei.Jo ports khule mile hain, unpar Nuclei ke network templates run karein taaki data leaks aur default passwords (admin:admin) mil sakein.Bashnuclei -l open_ports.txt -t network/ -tags default-login,misconfig -o network_bug


Step 1: Services aur Open Ports Find Karna (Naabu)
Kyunki in par HTTP (80/443) nahi chal raha, humein pata lagana hoga ki aakhir in par chal kya raha hai. Hum Naabu ka use karke top 1000 common ports scan karenge.

Bash
naabu -l non_web_targets.txt -top-ports 1000 -c 50 -rate 2000 -silent -o open_ports.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command check karegi ki kya kisi server par FTP (21), SSH (22), MySQL (3306), Redis (6379), ya MongoDB (27017) jaise ports khule hue hain. Results open_ports.txt mein subdomain:port format mein save honge.

Step 2: Automated Misconfiguration Testing (Nuclei)
Ab jo ports khule mile hain, humein un par default passwords ya known network vulnerabilities check karni hain. Nuclei ka network/ module iske liye best hai.

Bash
nuclei -l open_ports.txt -t network/ -tags default-login,misconfig -o network_bugs.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command bina brute-force kiye check karegi ki kya kisi FTP par anonymous login on hai, ya kisi database par bina password ke login ho raha hai. Agar koi bug milta hai, toh wo network_bugs.txt mein save ho jayega.

Step 3: Subdomain Takeover Check Karna (Nuclei)
In "non-web" subdomains mein se bohot saare subdomains aise honge jin par koi port open nahi hoga aur wo DNS level par dead honge (jaise kisi delete ho chuke AWS S3 bucket ya GitHub page ko point kar rahe hon). Yeh Subdomain Takeover ke liye perfect targets hain.

Bash
nuclei -l non_web_targets.txt -t takeovers/ -o takeovers_found.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command check karegi ki kya koi DNS record kisi aisi third-party service ko point kar raha hai jise aap claim karke company ka subdomain hijack kar sakte hain. Yeh bug bounty mein P2/P3 level ka critical bug hota hai.

